[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Hey, hey, hey. Welcome everyone. Welcome to Semifactory Nevada.'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Let\'s see. How about that? Kick things off.&nbsp; We got a little charge session going live&nbsp;&nbsp; outside. 1.2 megawws to help kick off the event.&nbsp; Welcome everybody. I\'m Dan Priestley. I lead the&nbsp;&nbsp; semi effort here at Tesla. And I\'m Lars. I lead&nbsp; most of engineering. Thank you so much for being&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here. It\'s awesome to celebrate this occasion&nbsp; and kicking open the factory and we\'d love to&nbsp;&nbsp; have Elon be able to do that too, but he\'s a&nbsp; little busy tonight. Yeah, I don\'t know if you&nbsp;&nbsp; guys saw on the news he wanted to be here, but&nbsp; unfortunately he\'s with the president and some&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'other folks. So, uh, he gave us a little message&nbsp; for you all. Welcome to the Tesla Semi event. Uh&nbsp;&nbsp; we\'re super excited to start production with the&nbsp; Tesla semi-truck and uh this is really going to&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'be a revolutionary truck uh that uh is capable&nbsp; of carrying the heaviest loads over very long&nbsp;&nbsp; distances uh with ease of recharge, mega charger&nbsp; that\'s capable of a megawatt of of power. Uh this&nbsp;&nbsp; is really going to be a phenomenal truck and it\'s&nbsp; going to be really also a driver\'s truck. Drivers&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are going to love driving this truck because&nbsp; it\'s it just has so much acceleration. Uh it\'s&nbsp;&nbsp; it\'s like almost like a sports car in truck&nbsp; form. So, it\'s uh it\'s going to be the funnest&nbsp;&nbsp; truck to drive. In the very near future, we\'ll&nbsp; be adding in the uh self-driving features. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'these will be incredibly important for for safety.&nbsp; Uh so, if somebody\'s on a long truck journey,&nbsp;&nbsp; uh they can uh engage the Tesla self-driving&nbsp; um and uh greatly improve safety and comfort&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of driving um so that the the driver arrives&nbsp; at the destination um and uh and still feels&nbsp;&nbsp; refreshed. Otherwise, driving for many hours&nbsp; straight can be quite exhausting. So, this is&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'really going to be a gamecher truck and and also&nbsp; it\'s going to make a ton of sense economically um&nbsp;&nbsp; because the cost of electricity per mile is much&nbsp; less than the cost of diesel, especially in these&nbsp;&nbsp; crazy times. So, I think this is really going to&nbsp; be something that works on on every level. Yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'d recommend placing more orders if you haven\'t&nbsp; already. Uh but the waiting list is already pretty&nbsp;&nbsp; significant. Um and this is really going to be&nbsp; a breakthrough product for for heavy shipping.&nbsp;&nbsp; Thank you and thank you for coming. Um and uh&nbsp; congratulations to the Tesla semi team uh Tesla&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'semi-engineering team and production team. Uh&nbsp; you guys have done incredible work bring us to&nbsp;&nbsp; this point. Um so well done. Thank you. You know&nbsp; we always start with the first principal approach&nbsp;&nbsp; but the battery line is the most automated line&nbsp; we\'ve ever made. As Dan said the cells don\'t get&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'touched all the way through but even to that. Um&nbsp; and and also this is the first time we\'ve done a&nbsp;&nbsp; powder coated a surface. So you can get a semi in&nbsp; other any color you want as long as it\'s white.&nbsp;&nbsp; for now. For now, but this did not start with this&nbsp; factory. It started again, we had some history,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'but we also knew that we needed to get some real&nbsp; field data, some real learnings. And we started&nbsp;&nbsp; a pilot fleet just under 200 vehicles to improve&nbsp; and learn. And I cannot thank those many of you&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are here tonight that helped make that effort&nbsp; possible and went along that journey with us&nbsp;&nbsp; as we introduced the first round of our class&nbsp; 8 truck. and we have been taking all of your&nbsp;&nbsp; feedback and learning. That fleet\'s been uh&nbsp; out there running, hauling freight every day,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'has now done 17 and a half million miles. And&nbsp; we\'re super proud of everything that it has done.&nbsp;&nbsp; And it wouldn\'t have been possible with all of our&nbsp; customers that have helped go along that journey.&nbsp;&nbsp; But we\'ve really listened and tried to make some&nbsp; improvements along the way. That\'s right. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as an engineer, nothing more is information&nbsp; is nothing more than the best knowledge you&nbsp;&nbsp; can have. and those, you know, 180 some trucks&nbsp; that you guys had and we had, we took all the&nbsp;&nbsp; learnings from that and the variety conditions you&nbsp; see here in the snow, in the rain, in the desert,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'climbing up Donner Pass, and we turned it all&nbsp; into what is now a better truck. Um, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp; we have demonstrated over 500 miles on a single&nbsp; charge. We\'ve demonstrated the reliability in&nbsp;&nbsp; the cold and everything, and we\'re putting that&nbsp; all into the improvements we\'ve made here. That\'s&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'right. So, ready for volume. What is it? what is&nbsp; this truck? And it really is designed for that and&nbsp;&nbsp; we\'ve changed. It\'s a lot easier to talk about&nbsp; the things that we didn\'t change. Uh but we\'re&nbsp;&nbsp; going to talk about things that we did change&nbsp; because we\'ve really touched a lot. And at the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'end of the day, it is more efficient. It is more&nbsp; reliable, more manufacturable, and ultimately set&nbsp;&nbsp; up to deliver the lowest total cost of ownership.&nbsp; And that\'s done through a variety of means. Um&nbsp;&nbsp; one of which is that we\'ve transitioned from our&nbsp; purchased 2170s to our in-housemade 4680s. That&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'allows us to do a lot of things with the battery.&nbsp; The battery is a heart of any electric vehicle&nbsp;&nbsp; and certainly the truck. It\'s allowed us to make&nbsp; the battery lower mass and lower kilowatt hours&nbsp;&nbsp; which means lower cost. But we also did that by&nbsp; improving efficiency around the entire vehicle. So&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'even though we have less battery in the pack, we&nbsp; have the same range. Yeah. And that\'s right. And&nbsp;&nbsp; that\'s 500 real world miles. Our customers have&nbsp; validated. We\'ve demonstrated it. You know, these&nbsp;&nbsp; are 82k fully loaded miles. Not diminishing load.&nbsp; We\'re not trying to cheat the numbers here. No,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for sure. I mean, and you can go maybe if you\'re&nbsp; half loaded 60,000 lbs, you can go 600 miles. So,&nbsp;&nbsp; we want to make sure that you guys understand this&nbsp; is no joke. This is the real deal and we\'ve proven&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it. Yeah. And the other thing is that range is&nbsp; great, but you don\'t just need range. You also&nbsp;&nbsp; need charging to go with that. We still charging.&nbsp; Oh, yeah. That whole thing that was live outside.&nbsp;&nbsp; Did we leave that truck plugged in? Yep. Oh, hey.&nbsp; Still 1.2 kilowatts. Like 12. Yeah. Still ripping&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '1.2 megawws. Yeah. Yeah. And that and that\'s&nbsp; really because of the work we did with the&nbsp;&nbsp; battery and the whole HV chain to make sure that&nbsp; the power can be there the whole time. So we\'re&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'at 27%. All right. So we also the other thing is&nbsp; that for those who have had a chance to review&nbsp;&nbsp; the vehicle over the years, you have mostly been&nbsp; familiar with long range, but we\'re super excited&nbsp;&nbsp; to also be building out of this factory multiple&nbsp; variants, including standard range, 325 miles of&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'capability, lower mass, great fit for a variety&nbsp; of applications. You know, obviously at Tesla,&nbsp;&nbsp; we care a lot about our customers. We care a&nbsp; lot about the people that are in our vehicles,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'not just from a safety standpoint and how they&nbsp; feel and how they operate, but like what kind&nbsp;&nbsp; of emotions they get when they\'re driving. And&nbsp; we wanted to make a truck that you don\'t have to&nbsp;&nbsp; sell someone to drive that they want to drive.&nbsp; And like I always say to my team, if you make&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'something that you want to drive, that people will&nbsp; follow you and want to drive. And this truck is no&nbsp;&nbsp; exception to that. Since the last truck, which is&nbsp; only four years old, we\'ve reduced the road noise&nbsp;&nbsp; orders. Well, not or magnetry, but some levels of&nbsp; percentage by adding acoustic glass and reducing&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cabin noise through extra insulation. And you&nbsp; know, sometimes when we do all that, we look back&nbsp;&nbsp; and we say, man, did we get everything right?&nbsp; Yeah, we don\'t always do that. We definitely,&nbsp;&nbsp; and this is where our customers said, nope, you\'re&nbsp; wrong. And we fully admit, we were wrong about the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[07:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'window. For anybody that interfaced with our&nbsp; old truck and tried the little pop out window,&nbsp;&nbsp; not sufficient. We\'re totally willing to&nbsp; challenge the spec and try something brand new.&nbsp;&nbsp; Turns out there\'s a lot of infrastructure in the&nbsp; world whether it\'s a badge reader or your toll&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[07:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'booth or you\'re talking to somebody on a call&nbsp; box. There\'s all kinds of stuff right at that&nbsp;&nbsp; height and it became evident that we needed a roll&nbsp; down window in order to make that infrastructure&nbsp;&nbsp; easier to interface with. Totally owned it. So we&nbsp; put one in. It\'s okay to be wrong, Dan. Yes. No,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[07:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'absolutely love to be wrong. But the other things&nbsp; you\'ll notice with our drivers here is that you\'ll&nbsp;&nbsp; see them they\'re incorporating a lot of features&nbsp; from our Tesla vehicles. You know, Luis when he&nbsp;&nbsp; gets into the truck clicks his own driver profile.&nbsp; And so if you buy a fleet of semis, you\'re going&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[07:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to actually be able to take every individual&nbsp; semi and make it that driver\'s semi right when&nbsp;&nbsp; they get in. Yeah. And this is like a nice visual&nbsp; where he clicks on his name. But in actuality,&nbsp;&nbsp; it\'s way more seamless than that because it\'s&nbsp; tied to their driver profile that\'s on their&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[08:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'phone. So when they walk up to that cab, when&nbsp; they open that door, the truck immediately says,&nbsp;&nbsp; "I am that driver\'s truck." It adjusts the seat&nbsp; settings, which is electronic. And so it knows&nbsp;&nbsp; exactly what your seating position wants to&nbsp; be. any other mirror memory, it\'s there. If&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[08:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you have any other profile settings in the UI,&nbsp; anything that you\'ve tweaked to your liking,&nbsp;&nbsp; it follows you truck to truck. Huge enabler for a&nbsp; fleet environment. Our firmware team\'s been doing&nbsp;&nbsp; that for years and it was no exception here.&nbsp; We\'re bringing in everything we\'ve had in the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[08:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'automotive fleet to the to the semi. We have trip&nbsp; planner so you can get updates on the fly. That&nbsp;&nbsp; means when you\'re driving, you don\'t have to worry&nbsp; about range anxiety because we take into account&nbsp;&nbsp; weather, traffic. If you do need to charge,&nbsp; we\'ll link you to a charger. And it doesn\'t&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[08:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just change based on weather and traffic, but&nbsp; because the semi has constantly varying loads,&nbsp;&nbsp; if you have an application where you\'re&nbsp; picking up new load or you\'re dropping it off,&nbsp;&nbsp; it adjusts dynamically based on your load&nbsp; to give you more accurate range estimates,'

[08:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'but it\'s out in the road. How does it do? Right?&nbsp; And we really put a high emphasis on maintenance.&nbsp;&nbsp; And we really emphasize again, best part is no&nbsp; part, best maintenance is no maintenance. But&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[09:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ultimately, the uptime is what really matters.&nbsp; And electric does provide that. But it\'s about&nbsp;&nbsp; proving it. Wherever we\'re going to put trucks,&nbsp; we will also have chargers. And we\'re putting mega&nbsp;&nbsp; chargers in the major regions and along major&nbsp; routes. And by the end of the year, we\'ll have&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[09:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'about more than 30 stations coming online with&nbsp; represent more than 200 megawatt capable posts.&nbsp;&nbsp; And in case you didn\'t think we could do this, we&nbsp; have over 80,000 superchargers worldwide. We know&nbsp;&nbsp; that when you\'re going to change an industry, you&nbsp; got to bring the ease to that industry. And we\'re&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[09:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'putting these in already. And it, you know, it\'s&nbsp; not just about our mega chargers that are going&nbsp;&nbsp; everywhere. It\'s also about, you know, private&nbsp; charging, overnight charging, and we\'re willing&nbsp;&nbsp; to do that, too. Yeah. And many of our customers&nbsp; are very interested in deploying charging at their&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[09:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'home base. It\'s the equivalent of home charging.&nbsp; That\'s great. Just like you have in your car,&nbsp;&nbsp; plug it in at home at the end of your day, end&nbsp; of your shift. And so, we\'re really excited&nbsp;&nbsp; because a number of players have already started&nbsp; ordering charge equipment. Either Tesla can help&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[10:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'at the installer, you can order it yourself. It\'s&nbsp; available on the website right now. And it comes&nbsp;&nbsp; in a couple different varieties. We have the Mega&nbsp; Charger, which is great for a number of fleets,&nbsp;&nbsp; particularly if you\'re slip seating or&nbsp; if you\'re trying to cycle trucks through,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[10:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'but often a offshift overnight charger is a&nbsp; better fit. And for that, we have our base&nbsp;&nbsp; charging product that\'s around 125 uh kilowatts.&nbsp; And so that\'s great for an overnight charge where&nbsp;&nbsp; you plug the truck, walk away. So excited to have&nbsp; everybody here. Thank you so much. But wait, wait,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[10:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'wait, hold on, hold on, hold on, hold on. Wait.&nbsp; Lars, did you have one more thing? You know, Dan,&nbsp;&nbsp; I think you\'re right. We can\'t have semi event&nbsp; without a Roadster. We\'ll see you next week.'
